   "evidence": "The temporary probe uses the real Semaphore and an injected clock/client matching ordinary endpoint replies, replacing the semaphore to simulate a restart. HEAD lines 271\u2013273 say `if (state?.expired && maxWait) { ... throw new Error(\"gate-slot lease expired\"); }`; the outer catch warns, then line 287 executes `return await work()`. That positive-budget fallback also exists at base, making it an explicit requirement gap. The zero-budget regression is introduced: HEAD enables unlimited responsive polling but retains the expired reservation ID; base instead reaches its deadline and falls back. Repeated expired replies cannot acquire capacity because heartbeat only looks up the forgotten ID."
