    "output": "maxWait 60000 exec 1 out [\"warning: gate-slot coordination unavailable: Error: gate-slot lease expired\"] reqs 3 [{\"name\":\"deploy\",\"immediate\":false},{\"id\":\"q\"},{\"id\":\"q\",\"release\":true}]\nmaxWait 0 exec 0 out [] reqs 21 [{\"name\":\"deploy\",\"immediate\":false},{\"id\":\"q\"},{\"id\":\"q\"},{\"id\":\"q\"}]"
   },
   "evidence": "At head, src/cli/gate-slot.ts:271-274 still has `if (state?.expired && maxWait) { ... throw new Error(\"gate-slot lease expired\"); }`, and the outer catch at 279-285 calls warn(e) and then runs work() unslotted. `id = state.busy ? undefined : state.id` (246) keeps the expired id. With maxWait 0 the expiry check is skipped, and `responsive` stops the deadline from ending the loop, so it polls {id:'q'} forever. At base, maxWait 0 sent immediate:true and hit pastDeadline right after the first reply, so it never hung. The unslotted run after expiry with maxWait>0 existed at base too, but #554 requires that a reachable daemon never leads to an unslotted run."
